{"skill":{"slug":"oracle","displayName":"Oracle"},"version":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1767652013275,"changelog":"","changelogSource":null,"license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":5806,"sha256":"183045d445482c95a1f4b81d87650bc9438ebf396cc8a92f05f9222f41c9efc6","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2177,"sha256":"7a6da08b2809908633f0d6c5f455a136966c48c0818afd41d8a550af4001f836","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789013598545,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"68cd715a31305f95e0fcbd5537bcad0a8d14b16796b1b56da09fdea75f097458","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/68cd715a31305f95e0fcbd5537bcad0a8d14b16796b1b56da09fdea75f097458","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: oracle\nVersion: 1.0.1\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to its reliance on `npx -y` to execute an external npm package (`@steipete/oracle`), which introduces a supply chain risk. It performs broad file access (e.g., `src/**`) and sends these files to external AI services via network calls, a high-risk operation despite explicit warnings in SKILL.md against sharing secrets. Additionally, the 'remote browser host' feature allows configuring a server to listen on `0.0.0.0`, which is a broad network exposure.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159621251},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1789013598545},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a disclosed helper for running an external review CLI, with normal but meaningful privacy and supply-chain cautions.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Browser automation, API calls, optional remote browser hosting, and sending selected repository files to external models are proportionate to the review workflow but require user attention to file selection and credentials.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The documented commands use npx -y @steipete/oracle without a pinned version, so users execute the currently resolved npm package rather than a fixed reviewed artifact.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The instructions emphasize user-selected file globs, dry-run previews, file reports, excluding secrets, and explicit consent for API runs that may incur cost.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill discloses stored Oracle sessions under ~/.oracle/sessions and long-running browser sessions; no hidden persistence, privilege escalation, or background installation behavior appears in the artifact.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to use @steipete/oracle to bundle prompts and selected files for a second-model review, and the documented capabilities match that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing or using this skill, consider pinning @steipete/oracle to a reviewed exact version or installing it through a locked project dependency. Use dry-run and files-report first, attach only necessary files, redact secrets, and be careful with browser sessions, remote-host mode, and API runs that may cost money or expose selected code to external model providers.","findings":"[T08] expected: The unpinned npx usage is real, but it is part of the disclosed purpose of invoking the Oracle CLI; it is best treated as a supply-chain caution rather than evidence of malicious or deceptive behavior.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789013598545}}}}}